{title: Because God Is Love}
{subtitle: 1 John 4:7–12}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 84}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Ebmaj7] | [Ebmaj7] | [Ebmaj7] | [Ebmaj7] |
| [Ebmaj7] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Nobody has seen the Father, [Gm7]nobody has seen his face
[Abmaj7]But love has come among us and it's living [Ebmaj7]in this place
He sent his only Son to us so we might live through him
[Gm7]That's how his love was shown to us, his love was shown in him
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Abmaj7]Dear friends, let us love one another
For love is from [Ebmaj7]God
[Abmaj7]Whoever does not love does not know God
Because God [Ebmaj7]is love
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
It was not that we loved him first, we never reached that high
[Gm7]But he loved us and sent his Son for our sins to die
[Abmaj7]So if God loved us like this, then we know what [Ebmaj7]to do
We ought to love each other like he loved me [Gm7]and you
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [Ebmaj7] | [Ebmaj7] | [Gm7] | [Gm7] |
| [Abmaj7] | [Abmaj7] | [Ebmaj7] | [Ebmaj7] |

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
This is love: not that we have [Gm7]loved God
[Abmaj7]But that he loved us and sent [Ebmaj7]his Son
As the atoning sacrifice for our sins
[Gm7]No one has ever seen God
But if we [Abmaj7]love one another, God remains in [Ebmaj7]us
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Because God is love
[Gm7]Dear friends, let us love one another
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
| [Gm7] | [Abmaj7] | [Abmaj7] | [Ebmaj7] |
| [Ebmaj7] | [Eb] |
